+## Summary
+
+One reviewer branch succeeded (QA). Two branches (security, architecture) failed during the parallel fan-out and produced no review artifacts. The surviving QA review identified a **HIGH** severity finding that directly nullifies the core intent of the implemented patch.
+
+---
+
+## Findings
+
+### HIGH — Schema and plan checks unreachable in full-mode validation
+
+**Reviewer:** QA  
+**File:** `.fabro/scripts/factory-validate.sh`, line 52  
+**Finding:**
+
+The new checks added in this pipeline run — eval schema presence/validity assertions and the `.factory/self/plan.md` artifact check — are located inside the `if [[ "$mode" == "--quick" ... ]]` conditional block, which terminates with `exit 0`. The `validate` workflow node executes `factory-validate.sh` without `--quick` (i.e., full mode), which means it takes a completely different code path and **never reaches these new checks**.
+
+**Impact:** The implementation's stated goal — "assert plan artifact presence in the implement → validate path" — is not achieved. Full-mode validation passes unconditionally without verifying that plan.md or any eval schemas are present. The quick-mode checks pass correctly, but they are only triggered by the `preflight` stage (which bypasses plan.md via `FACTORY_VALIDATE_ALLOW_MISSING_PLAN=1`) — not by the post-implement `validate` stage.
+
+**Required fix:**  
+Move the eval schema existence/validity checks and the plan artifact check outside of the `--quick` conditional block so they execute in both modes. Keep `exit 0` gated to `--quick` only so the quick path still short-circuits after those checks. Specifically:
+
+```bash
+# After the mode/log setup block, before the --quick exit:
+# 1. Check plan artifact (unless FACTORY_VALIDATE_ALLOW_MISSING_PLAN=1)
+# 2. Check all 6 required eval schemas exist and are valid JSON
+# Then: if --quick, exit 0; else continue with full workflow/cargo/bun checks
+```
+
+**Files requiring follow-up:**
+- `.fabro/scripts/factory-validate.sh`
+
